{"name":"Sea Lion","hex":"#7f8793","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea lion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pinniped of most genera in the family Otariidae (the eared seals).","A monster consisting of the upper part of a lion combined with the tail of a fish (a lion marined)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of sealion (“engage in disingenuous debate”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_lion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea lion","blocks":[{"text":"Sea lions are pinnipeds characterized by external ear flaps, long foreflippers, the ability to walk on all fours, short and thick hair, and a big chest and belly. Together with the fur seals, they make up the family Otariidae, eared seals. The sea lions have six extant and one extinct species in five genera. Their range extends from the subarctic to tropical waters of the global ocean in both the Northern and Southern hemispheres, with the notable exception of the northern Atlantic Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Steller_sea_lions_%28Eumetopias_jubatus_monteriensis%29_females_Tofino.jpg/330px-Steller_sea_lions_%28Eumetopias_jubatus_monteriensis%29_females_Tofino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_lion","wikidata":"Q3887135"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"},{"title":"Lion","blocks":[{"text":"The lion is a large cat of the genus Panthera, currently ranging only in Sub-Saharan Africa and India. It has a muscular, broad-chested body; a short, rounded head; round ears; and a dark, hairy tuft at the tip of its tail. It is sexually dimorphic; adult male lions are larger than females and have a prominent mane that extends from the head to the shoulders and chest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion","wikidata":"Q140"},{"title":"Lion (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lion is a color that is a representation of the average color of the fur of a lion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion_(color)","wikidata":"Q6555379"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Sea_lion_heart.jpg/500px-Sea_lion_heart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Sea_lion_heart.jpg/1280px-Sea_lion_heart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Sea_lion_heart.jpg/500px-Sea_lion_heart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea lion heart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASea_lion_heart.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t